  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 602.20 Functionally-equivalent use",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 602.20 “Functionally-equivalent use” means a use for a new or remodeled structure that:\n\n(a) Maintains the pre-existing use, for example using an existing residential structure as residential or an existing commercial structure as commercial; and\n\n(b) If not served by a public wastewater collection and treatment system, does not increase the sewage loading.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
